WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
- [Interviewer] Okay Fred, you ready?

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.131
- (silly voice) Cool, man!

00:00:02.131 --> 00:00:06.298
(series of sound effects: dog
bark, squeak, plane, whistle)

00:00:08.454 --> 00:00:10.952
(whistling, drum kit sounds)

00:00:10.952 --> 00:00:13.811
- [Interviewer] I'll take that as a "Yes.”

00:00:13.811 --> 00:00:15.912
This is Fred Newman.
- Hey!

00:00:15.912 --> 00:00:16.745
- [Interviewer] What do you do, Fred?

00:00:16.745 --> 00:00:19.508
- I honk for a living. (makes horn sound)

00:00:19.508 --> 00:00:23.016
I worked on a Nickelodeon
show called Doug.

00:00:23.016 --> 00:00:24.835
(playful music)

00:00:24.835 --> 00:00:27.885
I did the sound design and music.

00:00:27.885 --> 00:00:31.845
♫ Do-Da do-da-do-da do-da doo-a doo

00:00:31.845 --> 00:00:36.196
That wasn't Doug's voice,
that was actually my voice.

00:00:36.196 --> 00:00:40.254
We wanted to use as much as
we could household objects,

00:00:40.254 --> 00:00:41.854
things that a kid would have.

00:00:41.854 --> 00:00:44.676
Make it sound innocent
'cause this is a kid's diary.

00:00:44.676 --> 00:00:47.745
I tended to do a lot of
things with my mouth:

00:00:47.745 --> 00:00:50.796
(rhythm and musical sounds).

00:00:50.796 --> 00:00:53.254
- [Doug] Dear Journal,
have you ever been so broke

00:00:53.254 --> 00:00:55.489
you had to cash in your pennies?

00:00:55.489 --> 00:00:56.538
- [Interviewer] Not only did Fred work

00:00:56.538 --> 00:00:57.636
on the sounds and music,

00:00:57.636 --> 00:01:00.054
but was also a voice for
a bunch of the characters.

00:01:00.054 --> 00:01:04.785
- Porkchop the dog, (barks and whines).

00:01:04.785 --> 00:01:07.854
He would actually kinda
talk but not quite.

00:01:07.854 --> 00:01:09.505
"Roooorooo?"

00:01:09.505 --> 00:01:11.854
Skeeter.
- It's short for Mosquito!

00:01:11.854 --> 00:01:14.585
- Cool, man! You know, he
had the little honk (honks).

00:01:14.585 --> 00:01:15.505
"Hey, Doug! How ya doin’, man?"

00:01:15.505 --> 00:01:18.206
I saw he had a big nose; I
just thought he would always

00:01:18.206 --> 00:01:20.025
have this sort of adenoid thing going on,

00:01:20.025 --> 00:01:21.745
lot of post-nasal drip.

00:01:21.745 --> 00:01:23.703
Bud Dink--
- Welcome, newcomer!

00:01:23.703 --> 00:01:26.304
- Had big Chiclet teeth
(laughs as character)

00:01:26.304 --> 00:01:30.435
and his name was Dink because
of Double Income No Kids.

00:01:30.435 --> 00:01:34.905
The Beets: ♫ I've made more
allowance, yodel-ay-eee

00:01:34.905 --> 00:01:37.057
♫ Killer Tofuuuu

00:01:37.057 --> 00:01:39.996
And that was kind of based
on Sting a little bit.

00:01:39.996 --> 00:01:40.829
- [Interviewer] While Doug may be

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:42.479
Fred's claim to fame in our eyes,

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:45.639
he does all kinds of sounds
for movies, TV, and radio.

00:01:45.639 --> 00:01:47.668
His first movie was Gremlins.

00:01:47.668 --> 00:01:50.828
- I came and did the bad
guy, Stripe. (snarls)

00:01:50.828 --> 00:01:52.268
(snarling)

00:01:52.268 --> 00:01:56.047
Some of them are cute (speaking Gremlin)

00:01:56.047 --> 00:02:00.129
I did the sound when the Mogwai
turned into the bad guys.

00:02:00.129 --> 00:02:01.997
(wet bubbling and creepy oozing noises)

00:02:01.997 --> 00:02:03.191
- [Interviewer] But Fred's often on screen

00:02:03.191 --> 00:02:04.500
when you don't even realize it.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.292
- I did a lot of dogs in movies.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:10.172
I will go (dog whimper), you've gotta put

00:02:10.172 --> 00:02:14.943
real human emotions coming
out of animals or doors.

00:02:14.943 --> 00:02:17.401
The door has to sound
sad when you open it up.

00:02:17.401 --> 00:02:20.612
(creaking door)
That's where I get called in.

00:02:20.612 --> 00:02:22.559
- [Interviewer] Okay,
let's try a couple. Horse.

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:24.270
(heavy horse breathing)

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:27.101
Weasel.
(squeaking and squealing)

00:02:27.101 --> 00:02:30.641
Aliens?
(silly language)

00:02:30.641 --> 00:02:33.329
Birds?
(tweeting)

00:02:33.329 --> 00:02:36.616
Vibration?
- Ug-ug-ug-ug-ug-ug-ug-ug!

00:02:36.616 --> 00:02:38.129
(gentle piano music)

00:02:38.129 --> 00:02:40.272
The message I say is,
"Whatever makes you weird.

00:02:40.272 --> 00:02:43.731
"Go there. And pursue that." (bird calls)

00:02:43.731 --> 00:02:46.152
Mine is sound; I never
thought for a second I could

00:02:46.152 --> 00:02:48.701
do that for a living (bird calls)

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.112
but here I am!

00:02:50.112 --> 00:02:51.770
As the sun sinks slowly in the west,

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:54.070
we bid you all a fond farewell.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.403
(musical nostril tones)

